At Fri, 3 Mar 2006 13:50:25 +0100,
Juan Antonio Zapatero Campo wrote:
> 
> Hello all,
> first let me introduce a little bit what I am trying to do so that you can give me
> best help. I am building a onboard system for city-buses, which takes car of different
> tasks. Some of them are VoIP calling, audio reporting to passengers and external
> speaker. To make it possible through just one stereo soundcard, I need to force voice
> (the one caming out of alsa drivers) to go into one of stereo channels, let's say on
> the left one. Is there any way of performing this through the API?

So, you want to use a single stereo (interleaved) stream to split to
two mono streams?  Some hardware supports it on hardware, but many
don't.

A software solution is to run a dmix plugin as a backbone, then route
to left or right via route plugin.  If the realtime response matters,
it might be better to use JACK, though.


Takashi


